    "reasoning": "Each question's mathematical answer agrees with its own captured worked solution. No submitted grades or earlier answers are supplied; all MA findings below rely on worked solutions. q-210743: substituting u=ln(3x) gives 9∫u^(1/2)du=6u^(3/2)+C, equivalent to the selected square-root expression on the real domain. q-2194: u=ln x gives √2∫du/u=√2 ln|ln x|+C. q-31394: u=log_5 x gives (ln 5)u²/2+C. q-210751: u=log_5(x³) gives (ln 5)u²/12+C. q-31619: u=ln(5x) changes the bounds to 1 and 4, giving 6(√4−√1)=6. q-73657: u=log_8(2x) changes the bounds to 1/3 and 2/3, giving 3 ln 8[(2/3)²−(1/3)²]=ln 8. q-181791: the displayed integer lattice has −1≤x≤2 and −2≤y≤3. q-181805: the filled rectangle includes its edges and has 1≤x≤6 and 3≤y≤5, with real coordinates. q-182016: integer points lie on or above y=−1. q-181983: integer points lie strictly below the dashed line y=x−1. q-181690: the real strip excludes y=−2 and includes y=2, giving −2<y≤2. q-181600: the real region includes the solid line y=−x and excludes the dashed line y=2, giving −x≤y<2. q-181172: shading lies below the solid parabola, so real points satisfy y≤x². q-4782: integrating velocity gives x=−cos(2t)/2+C; x(0)=3 fixes C=7/2. q-102998: integrating acceleration and applying v(1)=6 gives v=3t²+3t³; integrating again and applying x(1)=2 gives x=t³+3t⁴/4+1/4. q-98753: f(y)>0 outside the roots and f(y)<0 between them, so arrows point away from y=2 and toward y=−4. Under the supplied source's classification, I is false and II and III are true. Every multipart field cites its question's complete final set expression, preserving all components in one contiguous source span.",
